# Loombre :: .dockerignore (repo root)
#
# Keeps the build context small — the Dockerfile's `pruner` stage does a
# full `COPY . .` (it needs the whole workspace to run `turbo prune`), so
# everything excluded here is bytes that never leave the host at all,
# rather than bytes that get copied and then discarded mid-build.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore's exclusions where they apply (build output, deps,
# local env/data) plus a few Docker-specific ones (.dockerignore/Dockerfile*
# themselves have no reason to be inside their own build context; .git
# history is never needed to build).

# VCS
.git/
.github/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# deps (reinstalled inside the build — see Dockerfile's builder/prod-deps
# stages; a host node_modules here would just be dead weight in the
# context, and could even be the WRONG architecture if this repo was ever
# `pnpm install`ed on a different host than the one running `docker build`)
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# build output (recompiled inside the build; stale host dist/ would only
# risk masking a real build failure by satisfying a later COPY with
# leftover files from a previous local `pnpm build`)
dist/
**/dist/
.next/
**/.next/
.turbo/
**/.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# env & local config — never bake secrets into an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
installers/docker/loombre.env
!installers/docker/loombre.env.example

# logs & scratch
*.log
**/logs/
coverage/
**/coverage/

# db local data / generated fixtures / reports (regenerated on demand,
# never part of a build)
.pgdata/
test-fixtures/media/
reports/
apps/worker/data/
perf/t0-baseline.json
perf/web-budget-result.json

# vendored ffmpeg (fetched fresh, checksum-verified, inside the
# ffmpeg-fetch build stage — see scripts/fetch-ffmpeg.mjs; a stale host
# copy here would bypass that verification entirely)
vendor/

# this lane's own worktree/smoke artifacts and docs never need to be IN
# the image being built
installers/docker/BUILD-NOTES.md
.claude/
